I am weird and reverse proxy everything by intercepting requests starting with `/strapi` in my through my SvelteKit `hooks.server.ts` rather than using something like nginx, but the effect is similar. I do this so that my main website and my admin panel are on the same origin without needing to put my SvelteKit deployment behind a reverse proxy too. But if you think it would be helpful for me to share an example, I am happy to create a version of my `hooks.server.ts` with only the relevant code.

<details>
<summary>How I did this from Strapi v5-v5.4</summary>

On the strapi server, I had this `src/admin/vite.config.ts`
```
import { defineConfig, mergeConfig, type UserConfig } from 'vite';

export default (config: UserConfig) => {
  const env = config.define!['process.env'];

  const strapiBackendPathname = new URL(env.STRAPI_ADMIN_BACKEND_URL).pathname;

  return mergeConfig(
    config,
    defineConfig({
      base: `${strapiBackendPathname}${config.base || ''}`,
      define: {
        'process.env': {
          ...env,
          ADMIN_PATH: `${strapiBackendPathname}${env.ADMIN_PATH}`,
        },
      },
    })
  );
};
```

And in my reverse proxy, whenever vite returned HTML, I would replace `<script type="module" src="/cms/strapi-` in the HTML with `<script type="module" src="/strapi/cms/strapi-` so that the main script that vite needs in order to start could be accessed. With the experimental release with the change from PR #22579, these are no longer necessary!

</details>

